{"seq":13,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T08:19:06.994Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"17b0f9c9b226cbef1be634bbf184758ee4a956d8b2394f819234c5f5c24c386c","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"Hi Dana, I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. #PD-4492. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md, dated 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments weren't reaching drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard. Support patched it at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the 04:00 shift got through the gate.\n2. #4419. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for firmware testing. This note has no date, so I can't tell when that happened.\n\nI also checked Moss's other notes. The 9/14 North pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal check-in both mention QFL but don't give a ticket number. The Central digests have tickets #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those belong to Central accounts, not QFL. One thing to watch for: Quarendon Freightways (one \"r\") is a different company and isn't a customer, so keep it separate in the notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
